{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Let your servant now speak a word</b> — meaning that he will speak few words, so they will not be a burden upon him. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that דָבָר (\"a word\") refers to the exchange that he entreats his face to substitute in place of Benjamin his brother, for he will not ask anything else of him, and the rest of his words are appeasement and entreaty for this matter:" "<b>And let your anger not burn against your servant</b> — he says: Let your anger not burn against me on account of my words before you." "<b>For you are like Pharaoh</b> — and with great awe I speak before you, as though I were speaking before Pharaoh."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:29.888305621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}